## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of core React Native list rendering, performance optimization patterns, and common mobile UX implementations.

## Key Concepts
- **FlatList optimization**: keyExtractor for stable identity, getItemLayout for skipped measurement, shouldItemUpdate for conditional renders
- **State management**: Handling refreshing, loading, pagination, and error states
- **Memoization**: Using React.memo and useCallback to prevent unnecessary re-renders
- **Error handling**: Implementing retry logic with exponential backoff or manual retry UI
- **Performance testing**: Frame rate monitoring, automated UI testing, and profiling on low-end devices

## Code Example
```javascript
import React, {useState, useCallback} from 'react';
import {FlatList, Text, View, ActivityIndicator, TouchableOpacity, StyleSheet} from 'react-native';

const ITEM_HEIGHT = 80;

const FeedList = ({initialData = []}) => {
  const [data, setData] = useState(initialData);
  const [refreshing, setRefreshing] = useState(false);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
  const [error, setError] = useState(null);
  const [page, setPage] = useState(1);

  const fetchMore = useCallback(async () => {
    if (loading) return;
    setLoading(true);
    try {
      const newData = await fetchData(page + 1);
      setData(prev => [...prev, ...newData]);
      setPage(prev => prev + 1);
      setError(null);
    } catch (err) {
      setError(err.message);
    } finally {
      setLoading(false);
    }
  }, [page, loading]);

  const handleRefresh = useCallback(async () => {
    setRefreshing(true);
    try {
      const freshData = await fetchData(1);
      setData(freshData);
      setPage(1);
      setError(null);
    } catch (err) {
      setError(err.message);
    } finally {
      setRefreshing(false);
    }
  }, []);

  const retry = useCallback(() => {
    setError(null);
    fetchMore();
  }, [fetchMore]);

  const renderItem = useCallback(({item}) => (
    <FeedItem item={item} />
  ), []);

  const keyExtractor = useCallback(item => String(item.id), []);

  const getItemLayout = useCallback((_, index) => ({
    length: ITEM_HEIGHT,
    offset: ITEM_HEIGHT * index,
    index,
  }), []);

  if (error && data.length === 0) {
    return (
      <View style={styles.errorContainer}>
        <Text style={styles.errorText}>{error}</Text>
        <TouchableOpacity onPress={retry} style={styles.retryButton}>
          <Text style={styles.retryText}>Retry</Text>
        </TouchableOpacity>
      </View>
    );
  }

  return (
    <FlatList
      data={data}
      renderItem={renderItem}
      keyExtractor={keyExtractor}
      getItemLayout={getItemLayout}
      onRefresh={handleRefresh}
      refreshing={refreshing}
      onEndReached={fetchMore}
      onEndReachedThreshold={0.5}
      ItemSeparatorComponent={() => <View style={styles.separator} />}
      ListFooterComponent={loading ? <ActivityIndicator /> : null}
    />
  );
};

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  errorContainer: {flex: 1, justifyContent: 'center', alignItems: 'center', padding: 20},
  errorText: {color: 'red', marginBottom: 10},
  retryButton: {padding: 10, backgroundColor: '#007AFF', borderRadius: 5},
  retryText: {color: 'white'},
  separator: {height: 1, backgroundColor: '#eee'},
});

export default FeedList;
```

**Performance Testing on Mid-Range Devices**:
1. Enable Performance Monitor in React Native Dev Menu
2. Test with Debug mode disabled (JS runs on device, not debugger)
3. Use automated testing with Detox to measure scroll performance
4. Monitor FPS during scroll - should maintain 60fps
5. Test with large datasets (1000+ items) to detect virtualization issues
6. Check memory usage to ensure proper list item recycling

